# User does not exist. Equalize response timing with the real-user path
# so an attacker cannot enumerate accounts via latency measurement:
# bcrypt.verifyPassword against the module-scope dummy hash forces the
# same ~250 ms cost-12 key schedule the matching path would have run.
# The return value is intentionally discarded; the result is "rejected"
# either way.
