# updated_at_ms is the same as created_at_ms for a fresh row; the SQL uses
# 6 params total because the schema has 6 columns being bound (user_id, title,
# body, priority, created_at_ms, updated_at_ms). Looking at the SQL again:
# "INSERT INTO todos (user_id, title, body, done, priority, created_at_ms,
# updated_at_ms)" - done is hardcoded to 0, so we have 6 bind params: 1-6.
# Param 5 is created_at_ms; we still need updated_at_ms at param 6.
storage local immutable bindIndex6 Int32 6
